  "estimatedSeconds": 90,
  "stem": "8% of the scratch cards sold at a shop in Kadoma win a prize. Chipo buys cards one at a time until she wins. Find the least number n such that the probability that she wins on or before her nth card is greater than 0.75.",
  "answerSpec": {
   "value": 17
  },
  "explanation": "$1 - 0.92^n > 0.75 \\Rightarrow 0.92^n < 0.25 \\Rightarrow n > \\frac{\\ln 0.25}{\\ln 0.92} = 16.6$. Check: $1 - 0.92^{16} = 0.737$, $1 - 0.92^{17} = 0.758$. So $n = 17$. (16 rounds down.)",
  "workedSolution": "1. $1 - 0.92^n > 0.75 \\Rightarrow 0.92^n < 0.25 \\Rightarrow n > \\frac{\\ln 0.25}{\\ln 0.92} = 16.6$. Check: $1 - 0.92^{16} = 0.737$, $1 - 0.92^{17} = 0.758$. So $n = 17$. (16 rounds down.)",
  "hints": [
   "P(X ≤ n) = 1 − 0.92ⁿ.",
   "ln 0.92 is negative: the inequality reverses."
  ],
  "modelResponse": {
